   "text": {
    "L1": "The Earth is our shared home. Small daily actions can help protect it.",
    "L2": "Some people think one person's actions do not matter. That is not true: repeated actions add up, and others can copy them.",
    "L3": "Refuse and reduce come first. Carry a cloth bag and a steel bottle instead of taking single-use plastic.",
    "L4": "If waste is made, reuse it before recycling it. Recycling still uses energy, and not everything gets recycled.",
    "L5": "A class of 40 students using cloth bags for 365 days could avoid about 14,000 plastic bags.",
    "L6": "A good plan is specific and lasts a set time. Use a seven-day chart and tick it each evening.",
    "L7": "Share the plan with family or friends. Sort waste, compost what you can, and never burn or bury plastic.",
    "L8": "Now put these three choices in order from best to least good for the Earth."
   },
